{# ── Hero stage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The motion is no longer a boxed illustration beside a text column: it is the
   hero's full field, and the copy sits on it. Everything that made the boxed
   version safe is kept.

   Poster-first by construction: the <source> elements carry data-src, not src,
   so a <video autoplay> with no resolvable source downloads NOTHING until JS
   decides motion is both permitted (not reduced-motion, not Save-Data) and
   needed (near the viewport, tab visible). Reduced motion, Save-Data and no-JS
   therefore cost zero video bytes rather than "load, then stop".

   The poster <img> carries intrinsic width/height inside a sized stage, so
   there is no black frame, no blank frame and no layout shift. The video sits
   on top at opacity 0 and is revealed only once it is genuinely playing, and
   it is inset by 1px so the poster stays strictly the larger element and
   therefore always wins LCP. Do not remove that inset without re-measuring.

   The tall 4:5 asset is selected on PORTRAIT phones only. A landscape phone is
   still under 860px wide, and cover-fitting the 4:5 frame into a 844x451 box
   scaled it 1.17x and cropped to the middle band — a full-bleed villa interior,
   which is exactly the real-estate read the composition must not have. Landscape
   takes the 16:9 asset, which needs almost no crop at that ratio.

   The stage is mirrored in RTL. The composition keeps its quiet negative space
   on one side and its built architecture on the other; mirroring puts the quiet
   side behind the copy in both scripts instead of dropping Hebrew type onto the
   brightest part of the frame. #}
<div class="hero-stage" data-hero-motion aria-hidden="true">
  <picture class="hero-stage-poster">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)" srcset="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-poster-mobile.webp" type="image/webp">
    <img src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-poster-desktop.webp" alt=""
         width="1280" height="720" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  </picture>

  <video class="hero-stage-video" autoplay muted playsinline loop preload="none"
         disablepictureinpicture disableremoteplayback tabindex="-1">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)" data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-mobile.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-desktop.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)" data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-mobile.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-motion-desktop.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>

  {# Two scrims: one along the copy edge for contrast, one at the foot so the
     stage resolves into the page instead of ending on a hard line. #}
  <span class="hero-scrim-edge"></span>
  <span class="hero-scrim-foot"></span>
</div>
